From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] configure: C33 FDPIC collects exception tables

GCC's probes for exception-table garbage collection link an absolute
address in .text, which an FDPIC link refuses; the linker collects the
tables correctly.  Answer them as for hppa-linux, so that a COMDAT
function's table goes in its group.

The generated configure carries the matching hunk, edited by hand rather
than regenerated; a submission regenerates it with autoconf 2.69.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>

diff --git a/gcc/configure b/gcc/configure
index 4a90e86..b821024 100755
--- a/gcc/configure
+++ b/gcc/configure
@@ -32881,6 +32881,10 @@ EOF
   rm -f conftest.s conftest.o conftest
 fi
 case "$target" in
+  c33-*-*linux*)
+    # FDPIC refuses the probe; the linker is right.
+    gcc_cv_ld_eh_gc_sections=yes
+    ;;
   hppa*-*-linux*)
     # ??? This apparently exposes a binutils bug with PC-relative relocations.
     gcc_cv_ld_eh_gc_sections=no
@@ -32933,6 +32937,12 @@ EOF
   fi
   rm -f conftest.s conftest.o conftest
 fi
+case "$target" in
+  c33-*-*linux*)
+    # FDPIC refuses the probe; the linker is right.
+    gcc_cv_ld_eh_gc_sections_bug=no
+    ;;
+esac
 if test x$gcc_cv_ld_eh_gc_sections_bug = xyes; then
 
 $as_echo "#define HAVE_LD_EH_GC_SECTIONS_BUG 1" >>confdefs.h
diff --git a/gcc/configure.ac b/gcc/configure.ac
index abf5e4f..3efa827 100644
--- a/gcc/configure.ac
+++ b/gcc/configure.ac
@@ -6249,6 +6249,10 @@ EOF
   rm -f conftest.s conftest.o conftest
 fi
 case "$target" in
+  c33-*-*linux*)
+    # FDPIC refuses the probe; the linker is right.
+    gcc_cv_ld_eh_gc_sections=yes
+    ;;
   hppa*-*-linux*)
     # ??? This apparently exposes a binutils bug with PC-relative relocations.
     gcc_cv_ld_eh_gc_sections=no
@@ -6299,6 +6303,12 @@ EOF
   fi
   rm -f conftest.s conftest.o conftest
 fi
+case "$target" in
+  c33-*-*linux*)
+    # FDPIC refuses the probe; the linker is right.
+    gcc_cv_ld_eh_gc_sections_bug=no
+    ;;
+esac
 if test x$gcc_cv_ld_eh_gc_sections_bug = xyes; then
 	AC_DEFINE(HAVE_LD_EH_GC_SECTIONS_BUG, 1,
   [Define if your linker has buggy garbage collection of
